Statements:
[
    "Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) techniques enhance the functionality of language models by integrating information retrieval from external sources.",
    "Two prominent methods of RAG are Naive RAG and Sentence-Window Retrieval.",
    "Naive RAG focuses on indexing, retrieval, and the generation of responses using large text chunks.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval optimizes the embedding and retrieval processes by managing smaller, contextually relevant sentence windows.",
    "Naive RAG utilizes a straightforward approach.",
    "Naive RAG involves indexing large text chunks or documents.",
    "Upon receiving a user query, Naive RAG retrieves the most relevant text chunk from the indexed documents.",
    "The retrieved chunk is then used directly to generate a response.",
    "Advantages of Naive RAG include simplicity and ease of implementation.",
    "Naive RAG has adequate performance in contexts where full contextual chunks are necessary.",
    "Naive RAG may struggle with factual accuracy when responses rely heavily on broader context.",
    "Naive RAG may generate responses from overly large chunks which can introduce noise.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval breaks down large documents into smaller, sentence-sized 'windows' during preprocessing.",
    "Large documents are split into individual sentences for retrieval in Sentence-Window Retrieval.",
    "When generating responses, Sentence-Window Retrieval fetches multiple consecutive sentences that are contextually relevant.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval provides a better basis for generating accurate and relevant responses.",
    "Key advantages of Sentence-Window Retrieval include enhanced context retention and improved response accuracy.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval reduces irrelevant information and noise by factoring in the surrounding context.",
    "Studies indicate that Sentence-Window Retrieval improves Answer Relevance by 22.7% and Groundedness by 38.2% compared to Naive RAG.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval reduces token generation in responses.",
    "Naive RAG is effective for scenarios requiring broader context but may adversely affect accuracy due to variable chunk relevance.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval significantly improves response relevance and groundedness by focusing on smaller, contextually coherent text segments.",
    "The choice between Naive RAG and Sentence-Window Retrieval should consider specific application needs.",
    "Sentence-Window Retrieval generally delivers superior performance in nuanced queries and contexts."
] 

